  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know that the product of numbers is even when at least one of the number must be even.</p><p>Hence total subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> in which product of numbers is even&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> Total subsets <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo></math> total subsets in which all the elements are odd</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>100</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>50</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>50</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>50</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>",
